-- title:
--   Geometric and adic fibres of the descended quotient map
-- statement:
--   The statement is an assembly of two fibre computations for the map $q$ that parametrises points of the quotient tower by Deligne data together with a coefficient homomorphism. The data and hypotheses are as follows.
--
--   **Base data.** A prime $r$; a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`) such that $\mathcal{O}$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), $\#(\mathcal{O}/\pi) = r$ (`hres`) and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal{O}$ (`hunr`); and a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is the fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficient ring.** A characteristic-zero domain `Onr` which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism `Fr`, subject to: $\pi$-adic completeness (`hOnr_complete`), maximality of the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_max`), the condition that every element of `Onr` satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), the condition that every monic polynomial over `Onr` of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and the congruence $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Write $\mathcal{O}_2$ for the equaliser of `Fr` followed by `Fr` and the identity, i.e. the subring of elements fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^2$.
--
--   **Determinant valuation.** A monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) with `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u \in \mathcal{O}^{\times}$.
--
--   **Group data.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, a subgroup $\Gamma \le G$ containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ scalar and $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma z) = 2$ (`hcent`) and an element $w$ with $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma w) = 1$ (`hodd`); a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by `hΓ'` as the set of $x \in \Gamma$ with $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma x)$ even. A homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}(2,K_0)$ with $\rho g$ the class of $\sigma g$ (`hρ`), such that the stabiliser in $\rho(\Gamma')$ of every vertex of the lattice tree of $\mathcal{O}$ in $K_0$ is finite (`hdisc`) and some finite set $S$ of vertices meets every $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit (`hcocpt`). An element $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ equal to the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`). A subgroup $N \le \mathrm{PGL}(2,K_0)$ with $N \le \rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNle`), with $N \cap \rho(\Gamma)$ normal in $\rho(\Gamma)$ (`hNnorm`) and of nonzero relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNidx`). A Mumford tower `DM` of type `MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`: schemes $Z_n$ with structure morphisms $\mathrm{zb}_n$ to $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$, transition morphisms $\mathrm{zt}_n$ realising $Z_n$ as the reduction of $Z_{n+1}$, properness and flatness of $\mathrm{zb}_n$, affine neighbourhoods of finite sets, and the chart maps $\mathrm{q}_n$ from Deligne data over $\mathcal{O}$-algebras killed by $\pi^{n+1}$ to $Z_n$-points, with their naturality, compatibility with the tower, $N$-invariance and open-immersion properties.
--
--   **The twisted tower.** Schemes $X_n$ with morphisms $\mathrm{xb}_n : X_n \to \mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ and $\mathrm{xt}_n : X_n \to X_{n+1}$; a finite group $G_2$ acting by $a_n : G_2 \to \mathrm{Aut}(X_n)$; morphisms $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n} : X_n \to Z_n$ and $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n} : X_n \to \mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1})$; a homomorphism $\theta : \Gamma \to G_2$; and $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphisms $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ of $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$. The hypotheses on these data are: each square $(\mathrm{xt}_n, \mathrm{xb}_n, \mathrm{xb}_{n+1}, \mathrm{Spec}$ of the truncation $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+2} \to \mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ is a pullback (`hcart`); $\mathrm{xb}_n$ is proper (`hproper`) and flat (`hflat`); every finite subset of $X_n$ lies in an affine open (`haff`); the action is over the base (`ha_over`) and commutes with the transition maps (`ha_xt`); $X_n$ is the fibre product of $\mathrm{zb}_n$ with $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the induced map $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1} \to \mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$, with projections $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$, $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ (`hX`); $\mathrm{xb}_n = \mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ followed by $\mathrm{zb}_n$ (`hxb`); the projections are compatible with the transition maps (`hxt₁`, `hxt₂`); $\theta$ is surjective (`hθsurj`) and $\theta \gamma = 1$ exactly when $\rho \gamma \in N$ (`hθker`); $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ is induced by `Fr` on $\mathcal{O}_2$ (`hFr₂`); the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ acts on the second projection through $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)}$ (`ha_pr₂`); and $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ acts on the first projection as $\sigma\gamma$ acts on Deligne data: if $B$ is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $\pi^{n+1} = 0$ in $B$, if $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ (that is, $P'(M)$ is the preimage of $P((\sigma\gamma)^{-1}M)$ under the base-changed lattice action, for every full lattice $M$), and if $x : \mathrm{Spec}\,B \to X_n$ satisfies $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ equal to $\mathrm{q}_n(P)$, then $x$ followed by $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ and then $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ equals $\mathrm{q}_n(P')$ (`ha_pr₁`).
--
--   **The quotient tower and the map $q$.** A datum `DQ` of type `TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`: schemes $Y_n$ over $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ with transition maps $\mathrm{yt}_n$ forming pullback squares, $\mathrm{yb}_n$ proper and flat, together with $G_2$-invariant finite surjective morphisms $p_n : X_n \to Y_n$ compatible with the towers, locally epimorphic, and satisfying the local universal property of the quotient. A family of maps $q$ assigning, to each $n$, each $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1} = 0$ in $B$ and each pair $(\psi, P)$ consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$ and a Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, a point $q_n(\psi,P) : \mathrm{Spec}\,B \to Y_n$; and the characterising hypothesis `hqdef`: whenever $\psi_2 : \mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1} \to B$ is induced by $\psi$ on $\mathcal{O}_2$, $P$ is a Deligne datum over $B$ and $x : \mathrm{Spec}\,B \to X_n$ satisfies $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ equal to $\mathrm{q}_n(P)$ and $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ equal to $\mathrm{Spec}(\psi_2)$, then $q_n(\psi,P) = x$ followed by $p_n$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions.
--
--   (i) *Geometric fibres.* For every $n$, every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $\pi^{n+1} = 0$ in $k$, and every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to k$: first, every $\eta : \mathrm{Spec}\,k \to Y_n$ whose composite with $\mathrm{yb}_n$ and with $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the structure map $\mathcal{O} \to k$ is of the form $\eta = q_n(\psi,P)$ for some Deligne datum $P$ over $k$; secondly, for Deligne data $P, P'$ over $k$ one has $q_n(\psi,P) = q_n(\psi,P')$ if and only if there exists $\gamma \in \Gamma$ with $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ related by the twisted action of $\sigma\gamma$, that is, $\psi = \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$.
--
--   (ii) *Adic fibres.* For every field $C$ which is a $K_0$-algebra, equipped with a valuation with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero, complete and algebraically closed; every commutative ring $R$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $C$ an $R$-algebra and the scalar towers $\mathcal{O} \to R \to C$ and $\mathcal{O} \to K_0 \to C$; and every pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi$ of $K_0$ in $C$ (an element of $K_0$ with $0 < v(\varpi) < 1$ whose powers bound the valuation of every nonzero element of $K_0$ from both sides): assume `IsAdicFrame π ϖ R`, i.e. $\pi$ is irreducible, $R \to C$ is injective with image exactly $\{c \in C : v(c) \le 1\}$, $R$ is $\pi$-adically complete, the elements of $K_0$ of valuation at most $1$ in $C$ are exactly those coming from $\mathcal{O}$, the image of $K_0$ in $C$ is closed, and $\pi$ and $\varpi$ have the same image in $C$. Let $\psi_0 : \mathrm{Onr} \to R$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map and assume `hmod`: $\pi^{n+1} = 0$ in $R_n := R/(\pi^{n+1})$ for every $n$, and write $\bar{\psi}_0^{(n)}$ for the composite of $\psi_0$ with the reduction $R \to R_n$. Then: first, for every family of morphisms $\eta_n : \mathrm{Spec}\,R_n \to Y_n$ such that each $\eta_n$ lies over the structure map (the composite with $\mathrm{yb}_n$ and with $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathcal{O} \to R_n$) and such that $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the transition $R_{n+1} \to R_n$ followed by $\eta_{n+1}$ equals $\eta_n$ followed by $\mathrm{yt}_n$, there exists an adic point $x$ of $\hat\Omega$ over $R$ — a family of Deligne data $x.\mathrm{pt}_n$ over $R_n$ compatible under the transition maps — with $\eta_n = q_n(\bar{\psi}_0^{(n)}, x.\mathrm{pt}_n)$ for all $n$; secondly, for adic points $x, x'$ over $R$ one has $q_n(\bar{\psi}_0^{(n)}, x.\mathrm{pt}_n) = q_n(\bar{\psi}_0^{(n)}, x'.\mathrm{pt}_n)$ for all $n$ if and only if there exists a single $\gamma \in \Gamma$ such that, for every $n$, the pairs $(\bar{\psi}_0^{(n)}, x.\mathrm{pt}_n)$ and $(\bar{\psi}_0^{(n)}, x'.\mathrm{pt}_n)$ are related by the twisted action of $\sigma\gamma$ over $R_n$.
--
--   This is the fibre description of the Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient map: the points of the quotient tower, at a fixed coefficient homomorphism from the unramified coefficient ring, are exactly the twisted $\Gamma$-orbits of Deligne data, both over algebraically closed residue fields and in the adic (compatible-family) setting. It packages [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_fib`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_fib) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_adicFib`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_adicFib) into the single conjunction used by the assembly statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib_of_mumfordTower_of_towerQuotientDatum`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib_of_mumfordTower_of_towerQuotientDatum).
